abstract: >-
  A spatially explicit modeling framework combining agronomic trial data,
  soil and climate layers, and predicted local input and output prices with
  a spatial copula Monte Carlo engine that jointly simulates seasonal
  rainfall and maize price, producing per-pixel profit distributions and
  risk-adjusted optimal fertilizer rates for maize across Sub-Saharan
  Africa under joint climate-price, climate-only, and price-only
  uncertainty.
keywords:
  - fertilizer profitability
  - yield response
  - risk analysis
  - Monte Carlo simulation
  - spatial copula
  - Sub-Saharan Africa
  - maize
  - smallholder agriculture
